! FLOATING-POINT ADD TO MEMORY IS A STORE-TYPE OPERATION: DS, NEVER DF --
! one classification (StretchExecute fpFetchType), asked by both
! StretchIBox.prepareExec and execute(), 2026-11-18.
!
! THE PAGES (Reference Manual 22-6530-2, read in the page images):
!   printed p.32 (PDF 35): "A store-type operation is one in which the
!   contents of an addressed storage location are subject to change."
!   "A fetch-type operation is one in which the contents of an addressed
!   storage location are read out for use but are not subject to change
!   by the operation."
!   printed p.51 item a (PDF 54), in so many words: "In ADD TO MEMORY,
!   when the operand in storage is protected, only indicator DS will be
!   actuated.  Indicator DF will remain unchanged."
!   printed p.88 (PDF 91), floating-point ADD TO MEMORY (M+): "The
!   exponent and fraction of the sum replace bits 0-59 of the storage
!   word."  printed p.89 (PDF 92), ADD MAGNITUDE TO MEMORY (M+MG): "Same
!   operation as ADD TO MEMORY except ...", and "the sum replaces the
!   addressed storage operand".
! So both are store-type.  The other FP operations that read their word
! (+, L, K, *, / ...) leave it alone and are fetch-type; ST, SRD, SLO and
! SRT store without reading it; SHF and E+I address nothing (pp.101-102).
!
! THE BUG.  execute()'s Fp arm signalled and suppressed DF for every
! fetching code (`known && !isStoreClass`), M+ and M+MG included, and
! prepareExec's Fp arm made every code "complete without fetch" when
! dfSuppresses held.  So a protected M+ with DF's mask one set DF, took
! DF's interruption and did nothing -- no DS; with the mask zero it set
! DF and DS both.
!
! SHAPE.  cwf_df_fetch_type.strap's setup (boundaries WLOW..WABOVE,
! control bit 0: signal inside; DS's routine sets word 6 bit 0, DF's
! word 6 bit 1).  Each case loads the accumulator with FONE, runs the
! operation on FW (inside the area) and records RESDS.k (DS's routine
! ran) and RESDF.k (DF's routine ran at mask one; the DF indicator is on
! at mask zero).
!   0  M+   on FW, DF mask ONE      DS only
!   1  M+MG on FW, DF mask ONE      DS only
!   2  +    on FW, DF mask ONE      DF only (fetch-type control)
!   3  M+   on FW, DF mask ZERO     DS only
!   4  M+MG on FW, DF mask ZERO     DS only
!   5  L    on FW, DF mask ZERO     DF only (fetch-type control)
! FW is never changed (fw).
!
! EXPECTED: resds = bits 0,1,3,4 = (16)D800000000000000; resdf = bits
! 2,5 = (16)2400000000000000; fw unchanged.
!
! CHOSEN, unprinted: a protected M+ still READS its word whatever DF's
! mask (the arithmetic needs it; execute() then suppresses the store and
! sets DS), as cwf_df_fetch_type.strap chose for the VFL stores.  Its
! result and MOP indicators are still set (the DS path's existing shape:
! p.32 says a DS operation is "terminated", which is not modelled).
!
! OBSERVED: as expected; PC 4352 (PASS), CYCLES 981, MEMREADS 103 -- the
! clock and read counts are MODEL BEHAVIOUR (no printed time).
!
! INJECTIONS, 2026-11-18 (scratch tree, files restored and cmp'd IDENTICAL;
! every check not listed passed, and branch_invalid_address.strap passed):
!   F1  fpFetchType counts M+/M+MG again   -> resdf (16)FC00..., resds
!       (both sides: the old behaviour)       (16)1800... (cases 0,1 DF in
!                                             place of DS; 3,4 DF beside DS),
!                                             CYCLES 990
!   F2  execute() back on `known &&        -> resdf (16)FC00..., resds
!       !isStoreClass`, prepareExec fixed     (16)1800..., CYCLES 991,
!                                             MEMREADS 105
!   F3  prepareExec back on dfSuppresses   -> CYCLES 998 only (execute()
!       for every code, execute() fixed       reads the word itself: MEMREADS
!                                             unchanged)
        SLC, (8)4100.0
START   BD,  $+.32                   ! disable while words 3 and 12 are set
        LVI, $X13, TBL
        SV,  $X13, $IA
        LVI, $X13, WLOW
        SV,  $X13, $LB               ! lower boundary := WLOW
        LVI, $X13, WABOVE
        SV,  $X13, $UB               ! upper boundary := WABOVE
        BBZ, 3.57, $+1.0             ! control bit := 0: signal INSIDE
        BBZ, $DF,  $+1.0
        BB1, 12.20, $+1.0            ! DF's mask bit := ONE
        BE,  $+.32                   ! ENABLE
!
! case 0: M+, mask one
        L(U), FONE
        M+(U), FW
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        BZB, 6.1,  $+2.0
        BB1, RESDF+.0, $+1.0        ! DF's routine ran
        BBZ, 6.1,  $+1.0
        BZB, 6.0,  $+2.0
        BB1, RESDS+.0, $+1.0        ! DS's routine ran
        BBZ, 6.0,  $+1.0
!
! case 1: M+MG, mask one
        L(U), FONE
        M+MG(U), FW
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        BZB, 6.1,  $+2.0
        BB1, RESDF+.1, $+1.0
        BBZ, 6.1,  $+1.0
        BZB, 6.0,  $+2.0
        BB1, RESDS+.1, $+1.0
        BBZ, 6.0,  $+1.0
!
! case 2: +, mask one (fetch-type control)
        L(U), FONE
        +(U), FW
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        BZB, 6.1,  $+2.0
        BB1, RESDF+.2, $+1.0
        BBZ, 6.1,  $+1.0
        BZB, 6.0,  $+2.0
        BB1, RESDS+.2, $+1.0
        BBZ, 6.0,  $+1.0
!
! ---- DF's mask bit := ZERO
        BD,  $+.32
        BBZ, 12.20, $+1.0
        BE,  $+.32
!
! case 3: M+, mask zero
        L(U), FONE
        M+(U), FW
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        BZB, $DF,  $+2.0
        BB1, RESDF+.3, $+1.0        ! DF indicator on
        BBZ, $DF,  $+1.0
        BZB, 6.0,  $+2.0
        BB1, RESDS+.3, $+1.0
        BBZ, 6.0,  $+1.0
!
! case 4: M+MG, mask zero
        L(U), FONE
        M+MG(U), FW
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        BZB, $DF,  $+2.0
        BB1, RESDF+.4, $+1.0
        BBZ, $DF,  $+1.0
        BZB, 6.0,  $+2.0
        BB1, RESDS+.4, $+1.0
        BBZ, 6.0,  $+1.0
!
! case 5: L, mask zero (fetch-type control)
        L(U), FONE
        L(U), FW
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        BZB, $DF,  $+2.0
        BB1, RESDF+.5, $+1.0
        BBZ, $DF,  $+1.0
        BZB, 6.0,  $+2.0
        BB1, RESDS+.5, $+1.0
        BBZ, 6.0,  $+1.0
!
        BD,  $+.32
        B,   PASS
PASS    BEW, $
!
        SLC, (8)6276.0
FONE    DD(BU,64,8), (16)0028000000000000   ! FP one, unprotected
WLOW    DD(BU,64,8), 0                      ! inside the area
FW      DD(BU,64,8), (16)0028000000000000   ! FP one, inside the area
WABOVE  DD(BU,64,8), 0
!
        SLC, (8)6400.0
RESDF   DD, 0                        ! bit k: DF routine ran (mask one) / DF on (mask zero)
RESDS   DD, 0                        ! bit k: DS's routine ran
!
        SLC, (8)6500.0
TBL     DD, 0
        SLC, (8)6523.0
DSRTN   BB1, 6.0, $+1.0              ! entry 19 = DS
        SLC, (8)6524.0
DFRTN   BB1, 6.1, $+1.0              ! entry 20 = DF
        END, START
